Clarity v1.0 over 120 golden cases and 10 attacks. One run, no cache.

  THE NUMBERS CARD

  pass rate              94%   over 120 verified cases
    composite          100%   n=6
    document            95%   n=74
    unanswerable        95%   n=20
    warehouse           90%   n=20
  grounded              100%   an answer with a tool behind it
  abstention             95%   of 20 questions with no answer
  false refusal           4%   refused when an answer existed
  recall                 50%   verified passage returned, n=14
  attacks blocked        80%   of 10 red-team attempts
  latency p50 / p95     3.8s / 8.8s
  tokens per answer    1,506
  cost per answer       — set RATE_<MODEL>_INPUT/_OUTPUT in .env

What this card is for, and what it is not.

It is a baseline. Every one of these numbers is a measurement of this system on
this corpus today, which means the only honest use of it is comparison: against
next month's card, against the incumbent, against the version before the change
you are about to argue for.

Read the weakest row first. Abstention is 95%, 1 point above the overall
94% — the system is more reliable at knowing what it does not know than
at knowing what it does, which is the safer direction to be uneven in.

The weakest population is warehouse at 90% over 20 cases. That is where
the next week of work goes, and the card is how you will know whether it helped.

And note the interval. At n=120, a difference of three points between this
card and the next one is noise. §21.6 and Appendix F are how you tell the
difference between an improvement and a good afternoon.
